          "description": "Judge whether each torrent can actually finish. `availability` is how many complete copies exist across reachable peers; when it does not exceed `progress`, no peer holds the missing pieces and the download can never complete however long it waits. Queued torrents are excluded because they report availability 0 simply for not being connected yet. `progress` is relative to the selected files, so `partial_selection` marks torrents that are 100% yet never fetched their deselected files.",
